From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dmayala <dmayala@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 18:21:15 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 0053] drm/a9_eink: bounded PG settle after a waveform (opt-in,
 a9_eink.pg_settle_ms)

R0 (2026-10-17) measured PG low at the end of a full-screen waveform that
was high again by the next sample; every rail fault so far was a low still
present 35+ ms later. A single instantaneous sample cannot tell a short
transient from a dropout.

pg_settle_ms (default 0 = off = the 0052 behaviour; clamped to 200): a plain
PG low (getter ok, pipeline on, valid PG descriptor, not forced off, no
emergency) read within pg_settle_ms after a waveform end is re-read about
every ms and counts as recovered only after TWO consecutive good reads
within pg_settle_ms of the first low. Anything else - no recovery in the
window, a low outside the window, a read error, forced/emergency, the gate
closing, the pipeline going off, or pg_settle_budget (default 3) recovered
dips already used in this HV session - latches exactly as before, from the
FIRST low sample.

1. a9_check_rail_sample(): settle line + return before the unchanged latch.
2. __a9_update(): after the 0052 wf-end read, a9_pg_wf_end() for a plain
   low at the waveform end (so a stuck low latches at once and a last
   waveform before the hold is covered); latched = the update aborts.
3. eink/rail_diag: one diag_settle line (attempts, recovered, timeouts,
   budget skips, recovered-dip duration histogram, longest). A9_DIAG_PD
   16 -> 12 to keep rail_diag well inside the sysfs page.
No FP9929A, transport, ring, guard, power-on/off, latch or cap change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/a9_eink/a9_eink.h     |  13 ++-
 drivers/gpu/drm/a9_eink/a9_eink_drv.c | 129 +++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 139 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

